{"abstract":[{"text":"Every simple path of a directed graph from a source to any of a set of targets, lazily, in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order a depth-first search from the source, taking out-edges in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges"},{"text":" order, reaches them.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/Iterator"],"anchor":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/maxLength"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/makeIterator()"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"generated":true,"title":"Type Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/Element"],"anchor":"Type-Aliases"},{"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/Sequence-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedSimplePaths"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DirectedGraph"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each copy of a parallel edge gives a different path. A path reaching one target continues to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the others, so a path through a target to another is listed after the shorter one. The source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"itself, when it is a target, gives the trivial path first."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The sequence holds the graph (a value), so iterating again gives the same paths. The first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"type":"text","text":" copies the rows the source reaches, O(n + m). A vertex that reaches no target is never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entered, but a partial path can still end where every way on is blocked by its own vertices,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the time between two paths is not bounded by a polynomial in n + m."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths"},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Traversal\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Traversal\/ST"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedSimplePaths"}],"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Traversal"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"SimplePaths.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Traversal\/SimplePaths.swift#L222"},"externalID":"s:9Traversal19DirectedSimplePathsV","title":"DirectedSimplePaths","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedSimplePaths","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure"},